icism, unorganized. B has reliability, stress handling, weather assessment, but pretentious, uncooperative, grumpy. A is reliable, quick decisions, positive crew atmosphere, but communication issues, egocentric, not willing to further education, no stress evidence. D has concentration, problem solving, responsibility, but hot temper, loner, weak leadership, no crew cooperation evidence.\n\nNow with Agent 2's shift, we need to decide. The panel still hasn't fully covered all criteria for C, especially crew cooperation and feedback. We have no explicit evidence for C's crew cooperation, but we have concerns: not open to new ideas, show-off, not good at taking criticism. That suggests potential issues with feedback and crew cooperation. B has documented stress resilience and conscientiousness, but also pretentious tone and uncooperative. However, we have no explicit evidence of B's crew cooperation beyond \"uncooperative\" and \"grumpy\". Actually the notes: \"Candidate B can be grumpy.\" \"Candidate B can be uncooperative.\" So B has explicit concerns about crew cooperation. C also has \"C is sometimes not good at taking criticism.\" \"C can be unorganized.\" Not directly crew cooperation but feedback orientation.\n\nThus both B and C have concerns. Which is stronger? B's stress resilience is critical for long-haul. C's technical strengths are strong. But lack of openness to feedback is a safety risk. B's pretentious tone may be less severe than C's resistance to new ideas. The panel may converge on B.\n\nAgent 1 should respond, perhaps acknowledging the arguments, and possibly shifting recommendation to B, explaining why B's documented stress resilience and reliability outweigh C's technical strengths given C's feedback issues. Or could maintain C if they think technical strengths outweigh. But given the panel now has two votes for B, and the shared mental model says not ready for convergence yet, but we can shift.\n\nWe need to produce a public message: \"I agree with Agent 2's shift to B because...\" Provide evidence: B very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, but also note concerns: pretentious, uncooperative, but these are less severe than C's lack of openness to new ideas and not good at taking criticism, which could hinder safety culture. Also note that we have no direct evidence of C's crew cooperation, while B's stress resilience is documented. So I will shift my vote to B.\n\nThus vote: Candidate B.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON."}
